{"kind":"request","text":"DX-C1: one span per judged act and per delivery, with a fixed attribute\nvocabulary. Child of 7558f46d (Hugh, 28 October) and an amendment of the\nobservability design (request 5a6f656a, note\nnotes/2026-10-12-observability-design.md).\n\nScope: items 1 to 5 of 7558f46d as written, fitted to what landed:\nthe metric sink and slot map of head 1 (e444edf8) already emit turn,\ndispatch and the other event kinds to the Analytics Engine binding with\nadopted or minted trace context. This head extends, not replaces: the\nturn event gains the missing attributes (definition digest, act kind,\nintent idempotency key, signer key id, answer, refusal reason and name,\nposition and hash when accepted, timed rules drained, commit duration);\ndispatch gains source position, send ordinal, target, attempt number\nand result; a read kind is added (read name, at head, complete flag);\nthe four counters and the duration histogram are derived in the sink's\nsummary rows; the trace context propagates on sends so a delivery's\nspan is a child of the sending act's span; no attribute carries field\nvalues, texts or member handles; the names and keys go in one table in\ndocs/operations.md as the stable vocabulary; the design note's slot map\nsection is amended in the same head.\n\nDone when: the witness of item 5 (one hosted MCP request yields one act\nrow and one delivery row with the listed attributes, the delivery's\ntrace parent being the act's span) and the vocabulary table.\n\nSize: medium. Order: after the journey view slices (MVP S4 and S6) and\nafter head 3's live calibration; grouped with the telemetry coverage\nwork (notes/2026-10-27-r14-telemetry-coverage.md). One gate, exact-head\nreview, PD-2 note.","body":{"conditions":"One gate, exact-head checker review, PD-2 note with the witness.","target_head":"0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d366